// A row-polymorphic helper whose every call is keyed to a twin: `pick` reads
// two fields of a nominal record and of an anonymous one, each call site
// proves its own layout, and nothing calls the base body — whose row never
// closes, so it can only floor.
//
// Contract (the frontier leg dead-base-unnarrated): the program answers 46
// and the compile says nothing about the base of `pick`. On boot c5439637 it
// answered 46 and narrated two unprovable-field-offset floors at stdin 0:0,
// a warning about a body the program never runs; the emitted reach keeps a
// decl only when a live reference reaches it.
type Person = {w: Int, x: Int, y: Int}

fn pick(u) = u.x * 10 + u.y

fn main() -> Int = pick(Person{w: 9, x: 2, y: 3}) + pick({x: 2, y: 3})
